  "worked_solution": "Let $({x}_{m},{y}_{m})$ be the midpoint between ${{(3a,-4b)}_{\u23df}}_{\\text{(}{x}_{1}\\text{,}\\,{y}_{1})}$ and ${{(-5a,6b)}_{\u23df}}_{\\text{(}{x}_{2}\\text{,}\\,{y}_{2})}.$\n\nWe use the midpoint formula as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}({x}_{m},{y}_{m}) & =(\\frac{{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}}{2},\\frac{{y}_{1}+{y}_{2}}{2}) \\\\  & =(\\frac{3a+(-5a)}{2},\\frac{-4b+6b}{2}) \\\\  & =(\\frac{3a-5a}{2},\\frac{-4b+6b}{2}) \\\\  & =(\\frac{-2a}{2},\\frac{2b}{2}) \\\\  & =(-a,b).\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
